{
  "id": "thought-insertion",
  "term": "thought insertion",
  "definition": "Thought insertion is a self-disturbance in which a person experiences thoughts as not arising from themselves, but as if they have appeared from elsewhere and may be attributed to an outside agent. It has been described as involving a break in the usual inner continuity of thinking, so that thoughts can feel unusually sensory or oddly salient.",
